    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "42c41a5b_c51c3e60",
        "filename": "cc/vendor_snapshot.go",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 204,
      "author": {
        "id": 1005967
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-04T22:10:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We should probably sync this with https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/build/soong/+/1371811.\n* The other change uses sanitized: { \u003csanitizer name\u003e: { src: }}}\n* The other change appends sanitized paths to the regular paths, and provides a special \"none\" sanitized option when you need exclusive-or. This matches the behavior of \"arch:\" and \"target:\" properties.\n\nI\u0027m not sure which approach is better. Neither works well with non-exclusive sanitizers (ex. cfi + integer).\n\nIt looks like this assignment will override all properties, not just \"src\". For example, in\nvendor_snapshot_static {\n    name: \"libfoo\",\n    src: \"libfoo.a\",\n    export_flags: \"-zzzz\",\n    cfi: {\n        src: \"libfoo.cfi.a\",\n    },\n}\nwill the value of \"export_flags\" be lost in the cfi variant?",
      "revId": "dfbac32d6b64d7d2a925b0dc9324e239b4de48c2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f7c6f320_faf4da5d",
        "filename": "cc/vendor_snapshot.go",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 204,
      "author": {
        "id": 1291338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-04T23:34:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Neither works well with non-exclusive sanitizers (ex. cfi + integer).\n\nWe don\u0027t need to think of non-exclusive sanitizers this time. We\u0027re explicitly stating that we don\u0027t support sanitizer on the vendor snapshot. The reason why we only capture CFI is that it can break in runtime, which AFAIK isn\u0027t the case for the other sanitizers.\n\n\u003e will the value of \"export_flags\" be lost in the cfi variant?\n\nYeah, it overrides all values related to library flags and it\u0027s intentional.",
      "parentUuid": "42c41a5b_c51c3e60",
      "revId": "dfbac32d6b64d7d2a925b0dc9324e239b4de48c2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    }
